1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,702
I have a prior commitment.

2
00:00:01,702 --> 00:00:05,439
We really should value our commitments.

3
00:00:05,439 --> 00:00:08,215
- Hey!
- I know you'll harass Bahay Aruga

4
00:00:08,215 --> 00:00:09,310
until you get their land.

5
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:11,679
A kid died there.
Do you have something to do with it?

6
00:00:11,679 --> 00:00:14,114
The theme is water goddess realness.

7
00:00:14,114 --> 00:00:16,884
I want it to be simple.
Didn't I tell you that?

8
00:00:16,884 --> 00:00:18,552
This is for us. We deserve it.

9
00:00:18,552 --> 00:00:20,921
I'm the one you'll marry, Hans. Not my image.

10
00:00:20,921 --> 00:00:23,357
How's your project with Joyce
in the orphanage?

11
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:25,859
There are lots to be repaired.

12
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:27,661
Why are they renovating it?
I'm already buying that land.

13
00:00:27,661 --> 00:00:29,496
I need to use force.

14
00:00:29,496 --> 00:00:31,632
I'm begging you. Leave us alone.

15
00:00:31,632 --> 00:00:34,668
Stop it.
You're doing that to scare the people off?

16
00:00:34,668 --> 00:00:36,470
Why don't you try me?

17
00:00:50,851 --> 00:00:52,386
Liam!

18
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:53,654
Liam, get out of there!

19
00:00:53,654 --> 00:00:54,788
- Mom, that's enough!
- Liam, get out of there!

20
00:00:54,788 --> 00:00:56,490
- Mom, let's stop this. Please.
- Madam!

21
00:00:56,490 --> 00:00:58,727
- No.
- Liam!

22
00:00:58,727 --> 00:00:59,861
Joanne?

23
00:00:59,861 --> 00:01:01,363
- Where's Liam?
- What?

24
00:01:01,363 --> 00:01:02,430
Liam!

25
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:03,732
Where are you, Liam?

26
00:01:03,732 --> 00:01:04,933
- Get out of there!
- Mommy!

27
00:01:04,933 --> 00:01:06,568
What's going on?

28
00:01:06,568 --> 00:01:08,203
- Well...
- Liam!

29
00:01:08,203 --> 00:01:11,907
- Liam.
- Joanne, Liam is not here.

30
00:01:11,907 --> 00:01:14,650
Don't hide your son.

31
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:18,079
First, your son poisoned my daughter's mind.

32
00:01:18,079 --> 00:01:20,916
And now, he's trying to have
an affair with her.

33
00:01:20,916 --> 00:01:23,885
That's how good your son is. He's so great!

34
00:01:23,885 --> 00:01:26,354
Watch your mouth!

35
00:01:26,354 --> 00:01:28,223
I didn't raise my son
to become a bad person.

36
00:01:28,223 --> 00:01:29,557
So stop!

37
00:01:29,557 --> 00:01:32,928
- What?
- You raised him to be a flirt.

38
00:01:32,928 --> 00:01:37,899
Your neighbors know that
he was born out of wedlock.

39
00:01:37,899 --> 00:01:40,268
You're way out of line!

40
00:01:40,268 --> 00:01:41,736
That's too much!

41
00:01:41,736 --> 00:01:44,038
You're too much!

42
00:01:45,473 --> 00:01:46,942
Aunt Tess, please stop!

43
00:01:46,942 --> 00:01:48,543
That's enough! Stop.

44
00:01:48,543 --> 00:01:51,112
Madam, stop, please.
That's enough. Please stop.

45
00:01:51,112 --> 00:01:52,814
Aunt Tess! Mom, that's enough!

46
00:01:52,814 --> 00:01:54,616
- Madam!
- You're so mean!

47
00:01:54,616 --> 00:01:56,751
How dare you come to my house!

48
00:01:56,751 --> 00:01:58,053
Mom! Mom! What's going on?

49
00:01:58,053 --> 00:01:59,721
Madam!

50
00:01:59,721 --> 00:02:00,889
What's happening here?

51
00:02:00,889 --> 00:02:02,757
- Wait, wait. Hold on.
- Oh my God!

52
00:02:02,757 --> 00:02:04,993
- What's this?
- A fight scene?

53
00:02:04,993 --> 00:02:06,494
You, you!

54
00:02:06,494 --> 00:02:07,896
You're all doing fine.

55
00:02:07,896 --> 00:02:10,432
But my daughter isn't!

56
00:02:10,432 --> 00:02:12,934
You're all great!

57
00:02:12,934 --> 00:02:15,804
You have no right to talk to me that way
in my own house!

58
00:02:15,804 --> 00:02:18,106
- Stop!
- Mom, let her be. Let it slide.

59
00:02:18,106 --> 00:02:19,441
Joyce, please!

60
00:02:19,441 --> 00:02:22,243
The nerve of your cheap mom
to come here and start a fight.

61
00:02:22,243 --> 00:02:25,180
Via, can you not?

62
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:27,349
Let's just help them fix things.

63
00:02:27,349 --> 00:02:28,817
Fix things?

64
00:02:28,817 --> 00:02:31,453
You started this mess.

65
00:02:31,453 --> 00:02:34,656
I didn't come here to fight, Via.

66
00:02:34,656 --> 00:02:36,691
Then let me start the fight.

67
00:02:36,691 --> 00:02:37,826
- Oh my!
- Via! Why?

68
00:02:37,826 --> 00:02:40,028
Why? I should have done that
a long time ago.

69
00:02:40,028 --> 00:02:41,129
Hey!

70
00:02:41,129 --> 00:02:42,630
Excuse me!

71
00:02:42,630 --> 00:02:46,935
Sir Liam stopped liking you
because you're a brat!

72
00:02:46,935 --> 00:02:49,304
- What did you say?
- Yes, you're a brat!

73
00:02:49,304 --> 00:02:51,139
Let me handle this!

74
00:02:51,139 --> 00:02:53,842
I've been holding back
dealing with this awful girl!

75
00:02:53,842 --> 00:02:55,310
Yes?

76
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:57,612
The design is so classy.

77
00:02:57,612 --> 00:02:59,881
But your attitude is bad!

78
00:02:59,881 --> 00:03:02,550
You're just a piece of trash.

79
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:04,517
What did you say?

80
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:10,125
I said, you're an ugly, atrocious trash!

81
00:03:10,125 --> 00:03:12,727
Hey. I...

82
00:03:12,727 --> 00:03:15,663
am not... trash!

83
00:03:15,663 --> 00:03:17,359
How dare you!

84
00:03:17,359 --> 00:03:19,834
Take it back. Take it back.

85
00:03:19,834 --> 00:03:21,780
Hey! You two, stop!

86
00:03:32,881 --> 00:03:34,281
Via...

87
00:03:35,650 --> 00:03:37,886
Via, please, let me explain. Let me...

88
00:03:37,886 --> 00:03:40,655
Let's talk. Hear me out.
I'll explain everything.

89
00:03:40,655 --> 00:03:42,912
Joyce, we talked already. Didn't we?

90
00:03:42,912 --> 00:03:45,160
We talked, lady-to-lady.

91
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:48,362
I asked you if you had an affair with Liam.

92
00:03:49,064 --> 00:03:50,887
You denied it.

93
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:56,570
Well... no mistress will confess.

94
00:03:59,874 --> 00:04:01,776
Joyce, let's go.

95
00:04:01,776 --> 00:04:04,019
Joyce... come on.

96
00:04:04,019 --> 00:04:05,213
- Liam, what are you doing?
- Come on. Come with me.

97
00:04:05,213 --> 00:04:06,113
- Joyce.
- Let's go!

98
00:04:06,113 --> 00:04:08,216
- Liam!
- Liam.

99
00:04:08,216 --> 00:04:10,118
Where are you taking my daughter?

100
00:04:10,118 --> 00:04:12,620
Liam!

101
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:15,689
Liam, what... what are you doing?

102
00:04:16,958 --> 00:04:18,026
Why are we here?

103
00:04:18,026 --> 00:04:20,061
Do you think running away
will solve anything?

104
00:04:20,061 --> 00:04:22,897
Joyce, tell me.

105
00:04:22,897 --> 00:04:26,233
- What's the meaning of what happened?
- I don't know!

106
00:04:27,735 --> 00:04:29,404
All I know is a lot of people
are getting hurt.

107
00:04:29,404 --> 00:04:30,738
So, this is wrong.

108
00:04:30,738 --> 00:04:32,073
Can't we make it right?

109
00:04:32,073 --> 00:04:34,375
How can we do that?

110
00:04:36,077 --> 00:04:40,881
Tell me, Liam. How can we make this right?

111
00:04:42,584 --> 00:04:47,354
With all the people you're hurting,
how can you make this right?

112
00:04:55,495 --> 00:04:58,865
Be thankful that you and Via
are still okay.

113
00:05:00,301 --> 00:05:01,503
Joyce, Joyce.

114
00:05:01,503 --> 00:05:03,737
What is it this time?

115
00:05:05,974 --> 00:05:07,574
Joyce...

116
00:05:09,644 --> 00:05:11,912
Joyce, I love you.

117
00:05:13,114 --> 00:05:15,249
I love you, but...

118
00:05:19,254 --> 00:05:20,600
But what?

119
00:05:24,292 --> 00:05:27,127
But I can't leave Via.

120
00:05:33,768 --> 00:05:35,326
Joyce, Joyce.

121
00:05:37,105 --> 00:05:40,107
The problem with you is your selfishness.

122
00:05:40,975 --> 00:05:42,644
You don't care about others!

123
00:05:42,644 --> 00:05:47,114
You make decisions based on
what's convenient for you, Liam!

124
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:51,786
You don't care about others.

125
00:05:51,786 --> 00:05:54,788
So, you deserve what you have right now!

126
00:05:54,788 --> 00:05:59,191
You're full of regrets
for the things you've done wrong

127
00:05:59,191 --> 00:06:01,993
because you can't stand by your decisions!

128
00:06:07,168 --> 00:06:10,838
You never bothered to take a leap of faith...

129
00:06:11,506 --> 00:06:13,640
Mr. Herrera.

130
00:06:44,439 --> 00:06:46,040
Who are you?

131
00:06:51,446 --> 00:06:53,915
I finally found you...

132
00:06:53,915 --> 00:06:55,482
Liam.

133
00:06:57,619 --> 00:06:59,119
Intoy?

134
00:06:59,787 --> 00:07:01,555
How are you, bro?

135
00:07:07,328 --> 00:07:09,263
Give it to me.
I need to do something about this.

136
00:07:09,263 --> 00:07:11,060
- Bro. Bro. Give it back.
- Intoy.

137
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,600
- Intoy, I need to do something.
- Give it back!

138
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,280
I have to do something with it, Intoy!

139
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:15,637
- Give it back.
- Intoy!

140
00:07:15,637 --> 00:07:17,104
I said give it to me.

141
00:07:17,104 --> 00:07:18,811
What's wrong with you?

142
00:07:20,942 --> 00:07:23,344
What's the matter with you?

143
00:07:23,344 --> 00:07:25,647
What do you want to change this time?

144
00:07:25,647 --> 00:07:27,615
Isn't it clear to you, Liam?

145
00:07:27,615 --> 00:07:30,118
There's a price to pay
whenever you use that typewriter.

146
00:07:30,118 --> 00:07:32,986
Intoy, what are you saying?
What's the price to pay?

147
00:07:34,455 --> 00:07:36,924
Everything's clear to me now, Liam.

148
00:07:41,396 --> 00:07:45,966
Our meeting wasn't an accident.

149
00:07:48,202 --> 00:07:50,604
Who are you? What do you know?

150
00:08:03,184 --> 00:08:05,786
I'm the owner of this typewriter.

151
00:08:11,993 --> 00:08:15,496
And whenever someone
uses this typewriter...

152
00:08:15,496 --> 00:08:18,665
I am reminded of my past...

153
00:08:19,534 --> 00:08:22,536
of my life story...

154
00:08:23,171 --> 00:08:25,973
and the curse of this typewriter.

155
00:08:28,543 --> 00:08:30,210
Intoy...

156
00:08:36,351 --> 00:08:38,752
I'm immortal, Liam.

157
00:08:44,392 --> 00:08:46,760
I've been alive for a long time.

158
00:08:47,729 --> 00:08:52,266
And I'm set to suffer forever
because of this typewriter.

159
00:08:52,266 --> 00:08:55,569
I used this for my personal gains.

160
00:08:56,537 --> 00:08:59,273
To ruin someone else's life.

161
00:09:02,310 --> 00:09:05,046
Intoy, Intoy, what are you talking about?

162
00:09:05,046 --> 00:09:06,914
Are you going insane?

163
00:09:12,362 --> 00:09:13,796
Liam...

164
00:09:15,556 --> 00:09:17,925
Let me show you.

165
00:10:04,834 --> 00:10:08,117
[Sabel, Diego]

166
00:10:09,043 --> 00:10:11,279
<i>There used to be a man
wearing a woven bag on his head</i>

167
00:10:11,279 --> 00:10:12,847
<i>during the Japanese occupation.</i>

168
00:10:12,847 --> 00:10:16,333
<i>He hides his face in that bag...</i>

169
00:10:16,333 --> 00:10:21,047
<i>so he can betray his fellowmen.</i>

170
00:10:21,047 --> 00:10:23,089
There are rebels here. Identify them! Hurry!

171
00:10:23,089 --> 00:10:24,519
<i>Did you know what he gets in return?</i>

172
00:10:24,519 --> 00:10:28,629
<i>A promise from the foreign invaders.</i>

173
00:10:42,376 --> 00:10:46,647
Don't kills us, please! Please, please.

174
00:10:46,647 --> 00:10:48,749
- Jose!
- Please, don't kill me.

175
00:10:48,749 --> 00:10:51,586
- Jose!
- Please, don't kill me!

176
00:10:53,875 --> 00:10:56,290
Jose!

177
00:10:56,290 --> 00:10:58,750
Sister!

178
00:11:09,136 --> 00:11:11,105
No, no!

179
00:11:11,105 --> 00:11:12,974
Don't believe him! No!

180
00:11:12,974 --> 00:11:16,430
How dare you! You're a monster! Animal!

181
00:11:18,846 --> 00:11:20,147
Don't!

182
00:11:20,147 --> 00:11:21,949
Animals!

183
00:11:36,497 --> 00:11:41,001
<i>Other Filipinos call him... a traitor.</i>

184
00:11:41,836 --> 00:11:44,304
<i>But behind that bag...</i>

185
00:11:44,939 --> 00:11:49,109
<i>the man they call a monster,
also has a heart.</i>

186
00:11:55,516 --> 00:11:57,017
Sabel?

187
00:11:58,753 --> 00:12:00,152
Sabel.

188
00:12:02,290 --> 00:12:03,991
Sabel...

189
00:12:03,991 --> 00:12:06,727
Please, take this.
You may have it for dinner.

190
00:12:06,727 --> 00:12:09,607
Can you please leave me alone, Intoy?

191
00:12:09,607 --> 00:12:11,866
Sabel, I don't have any bad intentions.

192
00:12:11,866 --> 00:12:13,667
That's enough.

193
00:12:14,335 --> 00:12:17,305
I just want to give you my harvest, Sabel.

194
00:12:17,305 --> 00:12:20,207
I already have a boyfriend, Intoy.

195
00:12:20,207 --> 00:12:26,647
I told you. I can never return your feelings.

196
00:12:26,647 --> 00:12:30,717
You should stop
or focus your attention on someone else.

197
00:12:36,724 --> 00:12:37,992
I'm sorry.

198
00:12:37,992 --> 00:12:40,293
I still have lots to do at home.

199
00:12:41,829 --> 00:12:43,564
Sabel, please.

200
00:12:43,564 --> 00:12:45,399
Please accept this.

201
00:12:45,399 --> 00:12:48,068
I harvested it for you.

202
00:12:50,938 --> 00:12:52,740
Hey!

203
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:55,843
Are you harassing my girlfriend? Are you?

204
00:12:55,843 --> 00:12:57,317
Diego.

205
00:12:58,512 --> 00:13:00,509
- What? Are you harassing my girlfriend?
- Diego!

206
00:13:00,509 --> 00:13:01,949
Diego!

207
00:13:02,650 --> 00:13:05,405
Diego, please. Stop!

208
00:13:05,405 --> 00:13:07,421
Diego!

209
00:13:07,421 --> 00:13:08,623
Are you harassing her?

210
00:13:08,623 --> 00:13:10,091
Diego.

211
00:13:10,091 --> 00:13:12,159
Diego! Diego!

212
00:13:12,159 --> 00:13:13,594
Let's go.

213
00:13:13,594 --> 00:13:15,495
That's enough.

214
00:13:20,201 --> 00:13:24,005
Stop. Stop it. That's enough, Diego.

215
00:13:24,005 --> 00:13:25,472
Let's go.

216
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:28,575
Enough.

217
00:13:56,704 --> 00:13:59,040
<i>The man wearing a bag in his head...</i>

218
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:06,213
<i>didn't notice that the anger
and the desire to be loved...</i>

219
00:14:07,214 --> 00:14:10,934
<i>had consumed him.</i>

220
00:14:10,934 --> 00:14:14,261
[Diego Ignacio]

221
00:14:15,256 --> 00:14:17,891
<i>And a monster was born.</i>

222
00:14:57,298 --> 00:14:59,599
Are all the names on this list?

223
00:15:01,435 --> 00:15:04,972
<i>He used the typewriter to get even.</i>

224
00:15:04,972 --> 00:15:08,576
<i>He let his feelings consume him.</i>

225
00:15:08,576 --> 00:15:14,415
Until his love turned into hatred and wrath.

226
00:15:14,415 --> 00:15:17,384
No, no, no, no. Please, please, please.

227
00:15:17,384 --> 00:15:21,055
Please, have mercy. Please, please.

228
00:15:21,956 --> 00:15:24,252
Sabel, leave.

229
00:15:24,252 --> 00:15:26,058
- Sabel!
- Please...

230
00:15:26,058 --> 00:15:27,628
You might get harmed.

231
00:15:27,628 --> 00:15:31,298
Please, please. Let go of him.
We are innocent.

232
00:15:31,298 --> 00:15:32,900
Please, please.

233
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:34,233
Sabel!

234
00:15:34,233 --> 00:15:39,173
<i>But the man wearing a bag in his head
did worse than betrayal...</i>

235
00:15:39,173 --> 00:15:42,910
<i>in his desire to get the woman he loves.</i>

236
00:15:42,910 --> 00:15:45,780
We're innocent. Please, let her go.

237
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:48,649
We're not rebels.

238
00:15:48,649 --> 00:15:51,152
Let her go!

239
00:15:51,152 --> 00:15:53,487
No! No, no, no.

240
00:15:53,487 --> 00:15:56,157
I'm begging you.
My husband and I are innocent.

241
00:15:56,157 --> 00:15:57,992
Are you sure?

242
00:15:57,992 --> 00:15:59,660
- No!
- Yes, I'm sure.

243
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:01,629
No. No, please.

244
00:16:01,629 --> 00:16:05,182
No. No, no, no.

245
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,158
Diego! No!

246
00:16:09,003 --> 00:16:11,705
Diego!

247
00:16:11,705 --> 00:16:14,542
Diego! Diego!

248
00:16:14,542 --> 00:16:18,512
Diego! Diego!

249
00:16:18,512 --> 00:16:22,683
You're a monster! Traitor!

250
00:16:22,683 --> 00:16:25,886
Animals!

251
00:16:29,745 --> 00:16:31,392
Sabel!

252
00:16:31,392 --> 00:16:32,738
You?

253
00:16:33,527 --> 00:16:37,665
You, monster! Traitor!

254
00:16:37,665 --> 00:16:40,167
Take this woman to the camp.

255
00:16:40,167 --> 00:16:41,569
No, no.

256
00:16:41,569 --> 00:16:43,704
We have a deal. She stays alive.

257
00:16:43,704 --> 00:16:45,206
We have a deal...

258
00:16:45,206 --> 00:16:48,876
You're heartless, Intoy!

259
00:16:48,876 --> 00:16:51,679
Animal! You're a monster!

260
00:16:51,679 --> 00:16:54,715
I can't let this woman live.

261
00:16:54,715 --> 00:16:56,584
No! Don't kill her! Don't kill her.

262
00:16:56,584 --> 00:16:58,219
Please, give her to me. No!

263
00:16:58,219 --> 00:17:01,688
Curse you, Intoy!

264
00:17:02,556 --> 00:17:09,396
You will pay for all your sins!

265
00:17:09,396 --> 00:17:14,201
A monster like you will suffer forever!

266
00:17:14,201 --> 00:17:16,703
You, monster!

267
00:17:19,373 --> 00:17:21,708
Sabel!

268
00:17:22,877 --> 00:17:25,078
Sabel!

269
00:17:30,751 --> 00:17:32,453
Sabel!

270
00:17:32,453 --> 00:17:34,388
Sabel.

271
00:17:34,388 --> 00:17:37,591
Sabel!

272
00:17:37,591 --> 00:17:39,894
Sabel!

273
00:17:39,894 --> 00:17:43,663
Sabel!

274
00:17:46,367 --> 00:17:51,104
The monster I'm telling you about
is here, Liam.

275
00:17:54,508 --> 00:17:56,776
I am that monster.

276
00:17:58,746 --> 00:18:02,115
Liam, I went crazy because of what happened.

277
00:18:04,852 --> 00:18:08,488
<i>I forgot about everything wrong that I did.</i>

278
00:18:10,357 --> 00:18:13,026
<i>I roamed the streets.</i>

279
00:18:14,628 --> 00:18:18,666
<i>I didn't notice that I don't age.</i>

280
00:18:18,666 --> 00:18:21,568
<i>I am immortal, Liam.</i>

281
00:18:21,568 --> 00:18:26,172
<i>I don't notice time passing by
because of my miserable life.</i>

282
00:18:27,841 --> 00:18:29,976
When I met you...

283
00:18:31,544 --> 00:18:34,961
it was not the first time
our paths have crossed.

284
00:18:34,961 --> 00:18:39,219
Something is pulling me closer to you.

285
00:18:39,887 --> 00:18:45,058
And that's because my typewriter
is in your family's care.

286
00:18:53,767 --> 00:18:57,871
Then we bumped into each other
under the billboard.

287
00:19:00,941 --> 00:19:02,542
You can have this.

288
00:19:04,445 --> 00:19:06,412
Thank you, bro.

289
00:19:10,351 --> 00:19:14,754
Does it mean the curse was passed on to me?

290
00:19:16,523 --> 00:19:18,536
You probably know now,

291
00:19:18,536 --> 00:19:23,430
that whenever you use the typewriter
to change your life...

292
00:19:23,430 --> 00:19:26,566
there will be a price to pay...

293
00:19:27,267 --> 00:19:31,138
just like when you first used the typewriter.

294
00:19:31,138 --> 00:19:35,476
You wished for Joyce to be happy.

295
00:19:35,476 --> 00:19:38,145
The wishes you wrote from your heart
came true.

296
00:19:38,145 --> 00:19:43,584
But your son with Joyce
disappeared in this world.

297
00:19:43,584 --> 00:19:45,299
Dex, your son...

298
00:19:46,053 --> 00:19:50,089
Along with it, as you climb to the top...

299
00:19:50,891 --> 00:19:52,393
it devours you.

300
00:19:52,393 --> 00:19:55,129
It makes you more greedy.

301
00:19:55,129 --> 00:19:57,998
You were able to abuse powerless people.

302
00:19:57,998 --> 00:20:02,736
Are you sure our farmlands won't be affected?

303
00:20:02,736 --> 00:20:08,731
Someone told me to ask you for a permit.

304
00:20:08,731 --> 00:20:10,744
Don't worry.

305
00:20:10,744 --> 00:20:13,781
I have my staff working on it already.

306
00:20:13,781 --> 00:20:15,815
But for now...

307
00:20:18,519 --> 00:20:21,021
please accept it.

308
00:20:21,021 --> 00:20:23,823
A little help from Casa Fuerte.

309
00:20:30,764 --> 00:20:32,866
Thank you.

310
00:20:32,866 --> 00:20:35,536
You're welcome, Mister Nestor.

311
00:20:35,536 --> 00:20:36,937
We'll go ahead.

312
00:20:36,937 --> 00:20:38,504
Be safe.

313
00:20:45,345 --> 00:20:49,015
<i>You sold your soul to the devil.</i>

314
00:20:50,651 --> 00:20:51,685
Is this complete?

315
00:20:51,685 --> 00:20:53,687
Yes, Boss.

316
00:20:53,687 --> 00:20:56,390
We'll be in trouble if something's missing.

317
00:20:56,390 --> 00:20:58,825
Boss, I'm sure it's complete.

318
00:21:00,527 --> 00:21:04,398
Big bro, I got the money.

319
00:21:04,398 --> 00:21:07,634
I will put it in Casa Fuerte.

320
00:21:07,634 --> 00:21:10,291
These are the memories
in the past seven years

321
00:21:10,291 --> 00:21:12,338
that I cannot remember.

322
00:21:13,126 --> 00:21:14,493
Intoy...

323
00:21:16,076 --> 00:21:18,745
is it true that I became an evil person?

324
00:21:18,745 --> 00:21:22,850
If you think that you're the only one
who became a monster

325
00:21:22,850 --> 00:21:26,320
for changing your life...

326
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:28,422
you're wrong.

327
00:21:28,422 --> 00:21:31,758
You created another monster.

328
00:21:31,758 --> 00:21:34,862
What do you mean?

329
00:21:34,862 --> 00:21:37,264
Ramon's henchman...

330
00:21:37,264 --> 00:21:38,898
Lando.

331
00:21:45,205 --> 00:21:47,540
Boss, I'm sorry.

332
00:21:52,207 --> 00:21:53,674
Sir, what's that?

333
00:21:55,115 --> 00:21:56,416
This?

334
00:21:57,451 --> 00:21:58,885
Coffee.

335
00:22:00,254 --> 00:22:02,089
- Stop him.
- Sir, hold on.

336
00:22:02,089 --> 00:22:04,124
What's inside your bag?

337
00:22:04,124 --> 00:22:05,925
Can I see it?

338
00:22:14,067 --> 00:22:15,636
Go ahead!

339
00:22:15,636 --> 00:22:17,270
Try to fight.

340
00:22:21,958 --> 00:22:24,711
Sir, it's positive.

341
00:22:24,711 --> 00:22:25,812
Okay.

342
00:22:25,812 --> 00:22:27,147
<i>Bring him to the police station.</i>

343
00:22:27,147 --> 00:22:30,366
<i>By simply bumping into him...</i>

344
00:22:30,366 --> 00:22:34,955
he was fated to get arrested
and change his ways inside the prison.

345
00:22:34,955 --> 00:22:37,957
But... what?

346
00:22:39,893 --> 00:22:41,061
You changed it.

347
00:22:41,061 --> 00:22:43,497
You changed the story.

348
00:22:43,497 --> 00:22:46,767
Lando's life changed too.

349
00:22:46,767 --> 00:22:50,304
Everyone who's getting off,
we've arrived in Huseña.

350
00:22:50,304 --> 00:22:52,405
Hurry up, get off.

351
00:22:54,841 --> 00:22:58,945
<i>You're the reason he was overcome by evil.</i>

352
00:23:00,414 --> 00:23:01,782
<i>You changed what was fated to happen.</i>

353
00:23:01,782 --> 00:23:06,386
<i>You were unaware that stories and lives
were affected by it.</i>

354
00:23:07,120 --> 00:23:08,622
Get in.

355
00:23:08,622 --> 00:23:10,357
Is there anyone else going to Segunda?

356
00:23:10,357 --> 00:23:12,025
Boss.

357
00:23:12,025 --> 00:23:14,593
- Is there still a seat?
- Yes.

358
00:23:17,349 --> 00:23:19,351
Segunda!

359
00:23:21,868 --> 00:23:25,438
He got into the bus that you were in.

360
00:23:26,707 --> 00:23:29,810
He stayed free. And continue doing evil.

361
00:23:29,810 --> 00:23:31,563
Until...

362
00:23:31,563 --> 00:23:34,840
<i>He became Ramon's henchman.</i>

363
00:23:40,921 --> 00:23:43,390
When you saw the typewriter...

364
00:23:44,654 --> 00:23:46,026
Bro!

365
00:23:49,196 --> 00:23:50,731
What did you do?

366
00:23:50,731 --> 00:23:53,867
You chose to bring Joyce back to life.

367
00:23:53,867 --> 00:23:56,136
Despite all my warnings.

368
00:23:56,136 --> 00:23:59,740
"Don't do it. There's a price to pay".

369
00:23:59,740 --> 00:24:01,874
Joyce came back to life.

370
00:24:03,406 --> 00:24:08,525
You wished Joyce wasn't
stuck in your messy life.

371
00:24:08,525 --> 00:24:12,983
<i>You didn't break up with your girlfriend.</i>

372
00:24:19,242 --> 00:24:20,609
Joyce.

373
00:24:21,428 --> 00:24:23,229
Hans?

374
00:24:25,333 --> 00:24:26,752
Surprise.

375
00:24:27,534 --> 00:24:29,870
- What are you doing here?
- Hello.

376
00:24:29,870 --> 00:24:31,872
I asked Miss Megan.

377
00:24:31,872 --> 00:24:34,274
She told me today is your big scene with...

378
00:24:34,274 --> 00:24:35,409
Josh and Maxine.

379
00:24:35,409 --> 00:24:39,346
So as a worried suitor,
I came here to make sure you're okay.

380
00:24:39,346 --> 00:24:41,415
Please keep safe.

381
00:24:41,415 --> 00:24:43,283
Hans...

382
00:24:43,283 --> 00:24:45,619
nothing wrong will happen to me.

383
00:24:45,619 --> 00:24:51,024
Especially now that the best defender
in the country is here.

384
00:24:51,024 --> 00:24:54,227
<i>You didn't tell Joyce your true feelings.</i>

385
00:24:54,227 --> 00:24:58,831
I need to talk to Hans.
Do you know where he is?

386
00:25:00,682 --> 00:25:04,824
I will tell you something important
about your investigation.

387
00:25:04,824 --> 00:25:09,142
The suspect in the murder of
the Casa Fuerte worker...

388
00:25:09,142 --> 00:25:14,514
The man we saw in the video,
caught by the CCTV camera...

389
00:25:15,248 --> 00:25:18,485
I know him. His name is Lando.

390
00:25:18,485 --> 00:25:20,287
It's Lando.

391
00:25:20,287 --> 00:25:23,290
That devil only works for one man.

392
00:25:23,290 --> 00:25:26,093
- Uncle, wait.
- Quiet.

393
00:25:26,093 --> 00:25:27,260
Hans!

394
00:25:27,260 --> 00:25:28,628
Hi.

395
00:25:29,329 --> 00:25:32,097
- Hey, Via.
- What are you doing here?

396
00:25:32,097 --> 00:25:34,568
Nothing. Taking time to relax.

397
00:25:34,568 --> 00:25:37,170
This is Uncle Edmond. Have you met him?

398
00:25:37,170 --> 00:25:38,338
Joyce's dad.

399
00:25:38,338 --> 00:25:41,274
Yes, you are Joyce's father. Right.

400
00:25:41,274 --> 00:25:43,477
Sorry, I saw you on the news.

401
00:25:43,477 --> 00:25:45,345
I'm Via.

402
00:25:45,345 --> 00:25:47,544
Liam's girlfriend.

403
00:25:50,183 --> 00:25:52,486
Do you want to watch Joyce on the set?

404
00:25:52,486 --> 00:25:53,687
Come on, I'll go with you.

405
00:25:53,687 --> 00:25:57,303
Yes, sure. Okay. Let's go.

406
00:26:00,023 --> 00:26:02,261
Uncle, let's talk about that in a safe place.

407
00:26:02,261 --> 00:26:05,040
- Let's go back to Manila together.
- Okay.

408
00:26:05,040 --> 00:26:07,874
I'll just talk to Joyce.
I'll say goodbye to her.

409
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:12,265
Papa...

410
00:26:15,308 --> 00:26:17,477
There's something you need to know.

411
00:26:20,714 --> 00:26:23,283
Joyce didn't know anything
about Ramon's evil doings.

412
00:26:23,283 --> 00:26:24,984
And because of that...

413
00:26:25,741 --> 00:26:29,249
Via and Lando didn't try to kill her.

414
00:26:47,574 --> 00:26:52,011
They targeted Edmond instead of her.

415
00:26:58,943 --> 00:27:00,121
Cut!

416
00:27:00,121 --> 00:27:01,422
Good take.

417
00:27:01,422 --> 00:27:03,982
Lovely. Perfect.

418
00:27:13,801 --> 00:27:15,302
Joyce...

419
00:27:16,637 --> 00:27:18,004
Good job.

420
00:27:23,876 --> 00:27:29,850
Edmond, the problem is
you already know too much.

421
00:27:29,850 --> 00:27:35,522
You should go blind.

422
00:27:39,132 --> 00:27:40,933
Blind?

423
00:27:44,131 --> 00:27:46,967
Lando, don't.

424
00:27:46,967 --> 00:27:48,569
You're a demon!

425
00:27:48,569 --> 00:27:50,237
Don't do it, Lando!

426
00:27:50,237 --> 00:27:51,739
Let go...

427
00:27:51,739 --> 00:27:53,373
Don't.

428
00:27:56,644 --> 00:27:58,645
It's too late for mercy.

429
00:28:17,598 --> 00:28:20,034
Remember when I asked you,

430
00:28:20,034 --> 00:28:23,403
if Joyce's death brought something good?

431
00:28:24,405 --> 00:28:27,674
She was able to send
all the culprits to jail.

432
00:28:28,843 --> 00:28:32,947
But because you altered the events
and brought Joyce back to life,

433
00:28:32,947 --> 00:28:36,016
the culprit remains free.

434
00:28:36,016 --> 00:28:39,219
The devil continues with his wicked ways.

435
00:28:48,395 --> 00:28:50,598
You don't want to give up
this orphanage, huh?

436
00:28:50,598 --> 00:28:53,634
Now, you'll be forced to leave this place.

437
00:28:53,634 --> 00:28:55,803
That's gasoline.

438
00:28:55,803 --> 00:28:57,538
Are you setting the orphanage on fire?

439
00:28:57,538 --> 00:29:00,006
Sister! Sister!

440
00:29:01,141 --> 00:29:05,479
Sister! Sister!
They're going to set the orphanage on fire!

441
00:29:05,479 --> 00:29:06,647
Sister!

442
00:29:06,647 --> 00:29:07,815
Ouch!

443
00:29:07,815 --> 00:29:08,816
- Let's go!
- Catch him!

444
00:29:08,816 --> 00:29:11,952
Help! Police!

445
00:29:11,952 --> 00:29:13,654
Help!

446
00:29:13,654 --> 00:29:15,623
Help.

447
00:29:15,623 --> 00:29:18,659
You got us tired.
You really want to be chased?

448
00:29:18,659 --> 00:29:21,428
You even bit me.

449
00:29:25,499 --> 00:29:26,834
What's happening to him?

450
00:29:26,834 --> 00:29:28,469
We don't know, Boss.

451
00:29:28,469 --> 00:29:31,005
He suddenly stopped running.

452
00:29:31,005 --> 00:29:33,940
Do you think he's having a heart attack?

453
00:29:36,277 --> 00:29:38,611
You should have stayed out of this, kid.

454
00:29:39,580 --> 00:29:41,982
Please, help me.

455
00:30:00,868 --> 00:30:03,269
Finish the job so we can leave.

456
00:30:09,143 --> 00:30:10,810
Mom...

457
00:30:17,818 --> 00:30:19,586
Forgive me...

458
00:30:20,287 --> 00:30:24,090
Forgive me, Sep.

459
00:30:26,318 --> 00:30:27,962
How dare you, Vergil.

460
00:30:27,962 --> 00:30:31,532
You're a monster. A monster!

461
00:30:31,532 --> 00:30:34,968
We both got addicted
to using the typewriter.

462
00:30:36,570 --> 00:30:40,340
We both used it for our own gains.

463
00:30:41,875 --> 00:30:43,142
Liam...

464
00:30:44,378 --> 00:30:46,379
You don't notice it, but...

465
00:30:47,348 --> 00:30:50,350
you're slowly becoming a monster.

466
00:30:55,756 --> 00:30:58,858
You have the same fate as mine.

467
00:31:04,098 --> 00:31:06,567
But now, Liam...

468
00:31:06,567 --> 00:31:09,469
you already know the price you have to pay.

469
00:31:10,437 --> 00:31:13,107
Like what happened to me...

470
00:31:13,107 --> 00:31:16,242
I was cursed to suffer forever.

471
00:31:17,378 --> 00:31:19,746
Liam, tell me...

472
00:31:20,447 --> 00:31:22,715
Tell me...

473
00:31:24,118 --> 00:31:27,187
that you still want to use this typewriter.

474
00:31:36,897 --> 00:31:40,234
I want to apologize.

475
00:31:40,234 --> 00:31:43,937
Honestly, I understand Joanne.

476
00:31:45,906 --> 00:31:49,209
She's just protecting her daughter.

477
00:31:53,580 --> 00:31:58,952
If only we could talk calmly,
I would tell her to...

478
00:32:01,288 --> 00:32:04,924
To let our children do what they want.

479
00:32:06,827 --> 00:32:09,462
Do you want it, Joyce?

480
00:32:13,801 --> 00:32:15,635
Want what?

481
00:32:16,670 --> 00:32:20,705
Do you and Liam like each other?

482
00:32:25,412 --> 00:32:28,449
Aunt Tess, about what happened
between Liam and me,

483
00:32:28,449 --> 00:32:30,083
about our...

484
00:32:32,086 --> 00:32:34,821
kiss.

485
00:32:37,157 --> 00:32:40,827
Sorry, Auntie, for not saying no.

486
00:32:44,932 --> 00:32:47,500
I didn't stop him.

487
00:32:49,303 --> 00:32:52,372
Maybe subconsciously...

488
00:32:52,372 --> 00:32:54,774
I wanted it to happen too.

489
00:32:57,377 --> 00:32:59,846
Even though I know it was wrong.

490
00:33:01,215 --> 00:33:04,184
You know, Joyce...

491
00:33:04,184 --> 00:33:05,852
nothing is wrong...

492
00:33:06,954 --> 00:33:09,489
when someone truly loves.

493
00:33:13,560 --> 00:33:18,331
But there's a right way to give in
to what the heart wants.

494
00:33:21,802 --> 00:33:24,938
I wish, somehow...

495
00:33:26,844 --> 00:33:30,380
you thought of the people who will get hurt.

496
00:33:32,746 --> 00:33:35,815
That's what we did wrong.

497
00:33:43,749 --> 00:33:47,886
Do you want me to talk to Liam?

498
00:33:50,664 --> 00:33:54,167
So you can correct everything?

499
00:33:55,435 --> 00:33:59,706
So you can explain to everyone who got hurt?

500
00:34:02,209 --> 00:34:05,845
So that you and Liam can be free?

501
00:34:18,796 --> 00:34:22,032
No one else should use this typewriter.

502
00:34:23,397 --> 00:34:26,599
How can you break free from the curse?

503
00:34:29,136 --> 00:34:30,937
I don't know.

504
00:34:32,039 --> 00:34:33,539
I don't know.

505
00:34:34,808 --> 00:34:37,610
Maybe I deserve to suffer...

506
00:34:38,278 --> 00:34:41,447
for all the wrong things I did.

507
00:34:53,894 --> 00:34:55,361
Joyce?

508
00:34:57,798 --> 00:34:59,599
Liam, son...

509
00:35:01,235 --> 00:35:03,069
What's going on?

510
00:35:09,343 --> 00:35:11,345
Mom.

511
00:35:11,345 --> 00:35:13,046
Joyce.

512
00:35:15,170 --> 00:35:17,504
I have something to tell you.

513
00:35:19,653 --> 00:35:21,788
Mom, please, sit down.

514
00:35:21,788 --> 00:35:23,290
Joyce, please, hear me out.

515
00:35:23,290 --> 00:35:24,524
Please, I'm begging you.

516
00:35:24,524 --> 00:35:25,925
Please.

517
00:35:27,127 --> 00:35:29,128
Come on, Joyce. Please.

518
00:35:49,316 --> 00:35:53,686
Good evening, Tess, Joyce.

519
00:35:54,354 --> 00:35:56,255
I'm Intoy.

520
00:36:16,843 --> 00:36:18,912
Hans.

521
00:36:18,912 --> 00:36:21,081
Hi.

522
00:36:21,081 --> 00:36:23,850
My fellow loser. Come.

523
00:36:25,272 --> 00:36:27,273
Sit, sit, sit.

524
00:36:32,592 --> 00:36:34,393
Wait.

525
00:36:35,095 --> 00:36:37,296
Why did you ask me to come here?

526
00:36:40,100 --> 00:36:41,667
No reason.

527
00:36:43,170 --> 00:36:45,538
I just want to...

528
00:36:46,773 --> 00:36:52,378
talk to someone
who's going through the same thing.

529
00:36:58,018 --> 00:36:59,597
I think you've had too much drink.

530
00:36:59,597 --> 00:37:00,754
Let's go.

531
00:37:00,754 --> 00:37:02,622
Let's go home. I'll drive you home.

532
00:37:02,622 --> 00:37:04,223
Hans...

533
00:37:06,259 --> 00:37:08,728
I have no one to go home to.

534
00:37:10,797 --> 00:37:13,567
Can't you join me?

535
00:37:13,567 --> 00:37:15,234
Even for a while?

536
00:37:29,583 --> 00:37:31,163
Let's drink.

537
00:37:32,919 --> 00:37:35,421
We'll show them...

538
00:37:36,923 --> 00:37:39,625
They can't be the only ones happy.

539
00:37:57,277 --> 00:37:58,645
I know this is hard to believe.

540
00:37:58,645 --> 00:38:02,582
But please, Mom, Joyce, believe me.

541
00:38:02,582 --> 00:38:05,384
I'm telling the truth. Please, believe me.

542
00:38:08,188 --> 00:38:13,493
Now, I get a grasp of everything I saw...

543
00:38:13,493 --> 00:38:17,002
that I couldn't understand.

544
00:38:19,533 --> 00:38:25,671
I saw that you and Joyce are married...

545
00:38:26,673 --> 00:38:28,808
and then...

546
00:38:30,143 --> 00:38:32,979
you have a child...

547
00:38:34,114 --> 00:38:39,118
who looks exactly like Sep,
but is named Dex.

548
00:38:40,654 --> 00:38:43,356
Are all of these true?

549
00:38:43,356 --> 00:38:47,227
- Are they?
- Mom... Mom...

550
00:38:47,227 --> 00:38:50,063
Mom, I'm sorry.

551
00:38:50,063 --> 00:38:51,864
But the truth is...

552
00:38:56,452 --> 00:38:58,153
The truth is...

553
00:38:59,421 --> 00:39:01,522
You were supposed to be dead.

554
00:39:06,079 --> 00:39:09,181
What do you mean?

555
00:39:09,816 --> 00:39:14,520
Mom, you didn't recover from your illness.

556
00:39:16,557 --> 00:39:18,791
You were supposed to be dead, Mom.

557
00:39:20,393 --> 00:39:26,032
But of all the changes I made...

558
00:39:29,269 --> 00:39:31,370
you're the only one who turned out right.

559
00:39:36,743 --> 00:39:38,678
And you, Joyce.

560
00:39:40,413 --> 00:39:42,449
Joyce?

561
00:39:42,449 --> 00:39:46,553
All your dreams, everything you saw,

562
00:39:46,553 --> 00:39:49,923
all your visions, they are all real.

563
00:39:49,923 --> 00:39:54,094
You died at the second revision of our lives.

564
00:39:54,094 --> 00:39:57,864
You died while we were filming.

565
00:39:57,864 --> 00:40:02,168
You learned about Congressman Ramon's secret.

566
00:40:02,869 --> 00:40:07,574
Uncle Edmond used to work
for Congressman Ramon.

567
00:40:07,574 --> 00:40:11,243
Uncle Edmond gave you that information.

568
00:40:13,113 --> 00:40:18,952
But because I used the typewriter,
everything changed.

569
00:40:18,952 --> 00:40:22,455
Everything changed. I saved your life.

570
00:40:22,455 --> 00:40:24,791
You didn't die.

571
00:40:24,791 --> 00:40:27,594
But there was a price to pay.

572
00:40:27,594 --> 00:40:34,434
I saved your life,
but they took it out on Uncle Edmond.

573
00:40:34,434 --> 00:40:36,636
He went blind.

574
00:40:36,636 --> 00:40:40,140
And in my desire
to bring you back to life, Joyce...

575
00:40:40,140 --> 00:40:42,475
Sep died instead.

576
00:40:45,312 --> 00:40:49,615
Sep died helplessly.

577
00:40:57,857 --> 00:41:01,761
Everything happened because...

578
00:41:03,330 --> 00:41:08,300
Because of that cursed typewriter
that our family owned?

579
00:41:12,038 --> 00:41:19,178
It's so hard to believe
everything you just said, son.

580
00:41:21,514 --> 00:41:23,649
But I know...

581
00:41:25,285 --> 00:41:31,358
I know that you won't make up
such a story, right, son?

582
00:41:31,358 --> 00:41:33,025
Yes, Mom.

583
00:41:48,375 --> 00:41:49,875
Joyce?

584
00:41:59,552 --> 00:42:01,854
Did I really die?

585
00:42:06,826 --> 00:42:07,994
I asked you before, Liam.

586
00:42:07,994 --> 00:42:12,198
I asked you if what I saw was true.
Did I really die?

587
00:42:13,233 --> 00:42:14,834
Someone killed Sep.

588
00:42:14,834 --> 00:42:20,005
They took it out on my father,
that's why he got blind?

589
00:42:26,244 --> 00:42:31,074
What if I want to file a case?
What should I tell the court?

590
00:42:31,074 --> 00:42:33,620
What testimony should I give them?

591
00:42:33,620 --> 00:42:36,790
That it was because of the typewriter?

592
00:42:36,790 --> 00:42:37,924
What do I tell them?

593
00:42:37,924 --> 00:42:42,661
That you did nothing wrong
aside from writing?

594
00:42:43,897 --> 00:42:45,998
I'm sorry, Liam.

595
00:42:49,936 --> 00:42:54,507
I want to believe you,
but my heart isn't ready yet.

596
00:43:07,721 --> 00:43:10,090
Excuse me. Aunt Tess, I'll get going.

597
00:43:10,090 --> 00:43:11,091
Joyce.

598
00:43:11,091 --> 00:43:12,725
Joyce.

599
00:43:26,306 --> 00:43:29,542
You know my biggest fear, Hans...

600
00:43:32,912 --> 00:43:35,080
is to be alone.

601
00:43:37,517 --> 00:43:40,320
Why would you be alone?

602
00:43:40,320 --> 00:43:43,322
Many people love and admire you.

603
00:43:46,292 --> 00:43:48,594
You really believe that?

604
00:43:51,331 --> 00:43:52,645
Yes.

605
00:43:55,268 --> 00:44:02,107
Can't you admit that your world
only revolves around Joyce?

606
00:44:03,143 --> 00:44:06,645
And then, poof!

607
00:44:07,347 --> 00:44:09,248
Just like that.

608
00:44:10,116 --> 00:44:14,086
In the blink of an eye, you lost her.

609
00:44:23,363 --> 00:44:26,465
Joyce and Liam will eventually
come back to their senses.

610
00:44:29,702 --> 00:44:33,005
Are we just going to wait until then?

611
00:44:33,873 --> 00:44:36,209
We can do something.

612
00:44:36,209 --> 00:44:38,545
So we can mark what's ours.

613
00:44:38,545 --> 00:44:40,012
Via...

614
00:44:42,082 --> 00:44:43,716
What do you mean?

615
00:44:45,485 --> 00:44:52,391
What I'm saying is
we have to fight for what's ours.

616
00:44:53,526 --> 00:44:56,695
We give our best for our relationship.

617
00:44:57,363 --> 00:45:00,332
They've just met.

618
00:45:01,234 --> 00:45:04,036
I want to love Joyce the right way.

619
00:45:06,642 --> 00:45:11,077
Hans, oh my God. Wake up.

620
00:45:11,077 --> 00:45:14,079
What are you talking about?

621
00:45:16,349 --> 00:45:19,786
I gave everything to Liam.

622
00:45:19,786 --> 00:45:25,625
I did everything for him.
Yet I was left alone.

623
00:45:25,625 --> 00:45:27,961
Don't be stupid.

624
00:45:27,961 --> 00:45:30,363
Hans, you have to fight.

625
00:45:30,363 --> 00:45:31,964
Come on.

626
00:45:42,876 --> 00:45:45,144
My half-brother, Vergil Herrera...

627
00:45:45,144 --> 00:45:47,947
He's the one who took over
my position in Casa Fuerte.

628
00:45:47,947 --> 00:45:50,049
All the money from all the illegal businesses

629
00:45:50,049 --> 00:45:52,685
of Congressman Ramon dela Peña

630
00:45:52,685 --> 00:45:55,554
is getting laundered in Casa Fuerte.
